        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friedrich Ratzel, László Deák\n- Organizations: Nazi Party\n- Concepts: Blood and soil\n- Topics: Nationalist ideology\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Ratzel, a Jewish geographer and ethnographer, became notable for first using the term \"blood and soil.\"\n- The slogan \"blood and soil\" came from the idea described in the chunk.\n- The Nazi Party supported the most extreme form of the \"blood and soil\" concept.\n- The Nazi Party continued supporting the most extreme form of the \"blood and soil\" concept until the end of the wars in which László Deák served.",
